TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"authorizedComments":[{"author":"uid:1000","body":"OVERSEER DIAGNOSIS (from your serve3 log, applies to current/future attempts): the engine dies in determine_available_memory with HIP OOM allocating EXACTLY 274877906944 bytes = 256 GiB = 2x total device memory (free 120.7 GiB, total 128 GiB). A 2x-total allocation in the KV-cache sizing probe is the unified-memory/GTT double-count signature on this APU: the fork carries a GTT-routed MemorySnapshot.measure specifically for this hardware, with kill-switch VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY=0. Set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY=0 in the serve env for the proxy first light (VRAM-only accounting is correct for the small proxy checkpoint) and retry; if that clears it, record the env choice in your receipt data and in the script so cp-proxy reproduces it. Do NOT chase this by shrinking gpu_memory_utilization — 0.6 of 128 GiB can never legitimately request 256 GiB; the measure is double-counting, the utilization knob is not the bug.","createdAt":"2026-08-29T10:06:55.172Z","id":5,"updatedAt":"2026-08-29T10:06:55.172Z","url":"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/5"},{"author":"uid:1000","body":"OVERSEER CORRECTION — SUPERSEDES the previous VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY steer (deep-dive verdict, log-verified). VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY=0 will NOT fix the OOM: your own serve log line 40 shows \"integrated_gpu=False\" — the APU accounting patches are already inert on this host and stock accounting is correct (total 128 GiB is real). The 256 GiB allocation is the VISION ENCODER PROFILING pass: \"Encoder cache ... profiled with 1 image items of the maximum feature size\" (log line 70) puts 65536 patches through the ViT as one sequence, and the math SDPA fallback materializes the [1,16,65536,65536] fp32 attention matrix = exactly 274,877,906,944 bytes (traceback: profile_encoder_cache -> F.scaled_dot_product_attention). FIX: add to the serve command: --limit-mm-per-prompt {\"image\":0,\"video\":0} (quote the JSON for your shell). This makes the model text-only: profile_run skips the encoder pass entirely and the API rejects image inputs instead of OOMing later. The bench targets are text-only; nothing is lost. Keep gpu_memory_utilization 0.6. Optionally export PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True (ds4-estate-proven). Do NOT use --skip-mm-profiling instead (a real large image at serve time would then hit the same wall). Record the flag in run-proxy.sh and the receipt so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it — the same flag applies to the big-model serve.","createdAt":"2026-08-29T10:15:42.127Z","id":6,"updatedAt":"2026-08-29T10:15:42.127Z","url":"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/6"},{"author":"uid:1000","body":"OVERSEER (ownership-failure insurance, same trap killed container-recipe attempt 1): your previous attempt did the work but exited WITHOUT committing — the driver fails uncommitted worktrees at ownership validation. Your final acts, in order, MUST be: (1) run the acceptance argv and see it pass; (2) git add ONLY paths in your conflict domains (scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, tests, results/receipts/proxy.json); (3) git commit; (4) verify `git status --porcelain` is empty before finishing. Context you inherit: the serve OOM is SOLVED — apply the --limit-mm-per-prompt {\"image\":0,\"video\":0} fix from the previous steer (text-only mode; the API rejects images; operator has ratified text-only for this campaign). The proxy checkpoint at /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy and the flashnext:dev image both still exist from prior attempts — do not rebuild what exists.","createdAt":"2026-08-29T10:27:57.768Z","id":7,"updatedAt":"2026-08-29T10:27:57.768Z","url":"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/7"}],"receipt":{"lateRecheckCommentIds":[],"preparedCommentIds":[5,6,7],"recheckTruncated":false,"rechecked":true,"source":{"kind":"local-jsonl","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl","preparedCursor":10,"recheckedCursor":10,"registrationId":"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae"}},"taskId":"proxy-tooling"}
